									"id" : "obj-15",
									"linecount" : 29,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 12.0, 15.0, 408.0, 395.0 ],
									"text" : "Version Updates:\n\nVersion 2.3.3 - November 1, 2014 - Recorded file's numbering now starts from 1, not from 2.\n\nVersion 2.3.2 - October 28, 2014 - I added the \"keystroke\" features to allow the simultaneous control of sounds.\n\nVersion 2.3.1 - (unreleased but improved.)\n\nVersion 2.3 - October 15, 2014 - The reset mechanism has been fixed, so that the sound will play in its entirety again (this bug occurred especially when the length of the loop-playback had been set to really short length!)\n\nVersion 2.2 - August 22, 2014 - I revamped the inner working of theplayback system.  Now the residual noise that occurs when the sound file is played backward.\n\nVersion 2.1 - July 4, 2014 - Happy Fourth of July! ... The bug that leaves out the last bit of the soundfile when played back, is now squished.\n\nVersion 2 - July 3, 2014: Clean-up on the start page.  Also, it now supports drag-and-drop file feature.  You can add your own custom sound to do looping. All files that are added will show up under the dropdown menu as \"CustomSound[X]\"\n\nVersion 1 - July 2, 2014: Application Launched.  The splicing feature is a bit buggish.  Not sure why there's some kind of residual noise that happens.  It does go away after clicking \"RESET\" and then hit the oval button."
								}

							}
 ],
