								"box" : 								{
									"bgcolor" : [ 0.501961, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 ],
									"fontname" : "Arial",
									"fontsize" : 12.0,
									"frgb" : 0.0,
									"id" : "obj-2",
									"linecount" : 20,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 488.0, 250.0, 472.0, 275.0 ],
									"text" : "DISCLAIMER:\n\nThis applicadtion is designed expressly for educational purposes only. This application is provided \"as is\" without warranty of any kind. I make no warranties, express or implied, that this application is free of error, or is consistent with any particular standard of merchantability, or that they will meet your requirements for any particular purpose. This application should not be relied on for solving a problem whose incorrect solution could result in injury to a person or loss of property. If you do use it in such a manner, it is at your own risk. I disclaim all liability for direct, indirect, or consequential damages resulting from your use of the application.\n\n\nCOPYRIGHT ISSUE:\n\nThis application allows you to use your own sound, and it even allows you to record your creations.  When you use your own sound as you create your mix, be absolutely sure that you are using the sounds that you yourself can claim to be the owner of.  Do not use files that are someone else's.  The same goes for the sound files on the internet whose  ownership is obscure.  I disclaim the responsibility in case of trouble for copyright infringement.  So do not get into one!",
									"textcolor" : [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"bgcolor" : [ 1.0, 0.501961, 0.0, 0.29 ],
									"fontname" : "Arial",
									"fontsize" : 12.0,
									"frgb" : 0.0,
									"id" : "obj-1",
									"linecount" : 24,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 15.0, 382.0, 470.0, 328.0 ],
									"text" : "NOTICE:\n\nThis application was made with Max 6.\n\nThis application is free of charge.  I would be glad to see people using it, being curious about different kinds of sound, and doing some creative things with this application. \n\nIf you are an educator and use this application in your classroom, just as this application was originally conceived to be used in the class I was teaching, I would be curious to know how you are using it, and how your students reacted!  \n\nLikewise, if you are a creator and if you happen to use this software, drop me an email (though you shouldn't feel obligated to send your music)..  I'd be happy to know that I made something useful.\n\nComments and requests about the future versions of this application, feel free to drop an email, though I can't guarantee that all your requests will be accommodated.\n\nPlease follow the following Creative Commons License protocol.\n\nThis work is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. To view a copy of this license, visit http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.\n "
								}

							}
, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"bgcolor" : [ 1.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.19 ],
									"fontname" : "Arial",
									"fontsize" : 12.0,
									"frgb" : 0.0,
									"id" : "obj-15",
									"linecount" : 26,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 15.0, 16.0, 470.0, 355.0 ],
									"text" : "ABOUT:\n\nThis standalone application was made possible with the sonic contributions from the students of the 2014 Summer Music Humanities, §11 at Columbia University, New York.  \n\nThis application is a re-imagining of the musique concrète, as well as\nsome of the tape techniques such as looping.  \n\nIn the subpatch \"MIRA,\" select four sounds, loop them as you like, push the oval buttons for single-sound playbacks, and there are slides for speed/pitch, as well as panning.  You can also record the interactions as well, and the file should appear as \"sound[number].wav\" under the same folder where the application is located.\n\nIf you have a sound you want to use, drop your soundfiles (.aiff or .wav format) onto the green box in the \"MIRA\" subpatch.\n\nWhile it is recommended that you use this application with the \"Mira\" app for iPad (available from Cycling '74), it is completely optional.\n\nHave fun!  \n\nYoshiaki Onishi, composer\nhttp://www.yoshionishi.com\ninfo [at] yoshionishi.com\n "
								}

							}
 ],
